---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Ybor — The delivery system for enterprise software at AI speed"
  description="AI writes code faster than most teams can ship it. Ybor closes the gap — production Kubernetes on AWS, Azure, and GCP, commit to live in minutes. SOC 2® report. Built on open source."
>
<style slot="head">
  /* Outcomes metric cards — built from Ybor tokens */
  .mstats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 20px; margin-top: 56px; }
  .mc { background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--neutral-100); border-radius: var(--r-xl); padding: 28px 26px 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .mc-fig { font-size: 46px; line-height: 1; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.04em; color: var(--ink); }
  .mc-lbl { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--neutral-700); margin-top: 12px; font-weight: 500; }
  .mc-src { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--neutral-500); margin-top: 20px; padding-top: 14px; border-top: 1px solid var(--stroke-light); }
  .mc.c-purple { --mc-accent: var(--purple); --mc-tint: var(--purple-tint); }
  .mc.c-green  { --mc-accent: var(--green-dark); --mc-tint: #E9F9EA; }
  .mc.c-orange { --mc-accent: var(--orange-dark); --mc-tint: #FBEDE4; }
  /* Dark mode: Astro scopes these page rules, raising their specificity enough to
     override the design system's dark .mc treatment (leaving the cards white).
     Re-apply the dark surfaces/text/accents so the stat cards read correctly. */
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .mc { background: var(--surface-2); border-color: var(--border-d); }
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .mc-fig { color: var(--text-0); }
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .mc-lbl { color: var(--text-1); }
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .mc-src { color: var(--text-2); border-top-color: var(--border-d); }
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .mc.c-purple { --mc-accent: #A98AE6; --mc-tint: rgba(140,100,218,0.22); }
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .mc.c-green  { --mc-accent: #3CCB86; --mc-tint: rgba(60,203,134,0.18); }
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .mc.c-orange { --mc-accent: #F08A47; --mc-tint: rgba(240,138,71,0.18); }
  /* stat movement — animates once on scroll-in */
  .mc-viz { height: 10px; display: flex; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 26px; }
  .mc-bar { position: relative; width: 100%; height: 10px; border-radius: var(--r-full); background: var(--mc-tint); overflow: hidden; }
  .mc-bar::after { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; bottom: 0; width: 0; background: var(--mc-accent); border-radius: inherit; transition: width 1s cubic-bezier(.22,.61,.36,1); }
  .mc.in .mc-bar::after { width: var(--to); }
  .mc-seg { display: flex; gap: 7px; width: 100%; }
  .mc-seg span { position: relative; flex: 1; height: 10px; border-radius: var(--r-full); background: var(--mc-tint); overflow: hidden; }
  .mc-seg span::after { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 0; background: var(--mc-accent); border-radius: inherit; transition: width .55s cubic-bezier(.22,.61,.36,1); }
  .mc.in .mc-seg span::after { width: 100%; }
  .mc.in .mc-seg span:nth-child(2)::after { transition-delay: .15s; }
  .mc.in .mc-seg span:nth-child(3)::after { transition-delay: .3s; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .mc-bar::after { transition: none; width: var(--to); }
    .mc-seg span::after { transition: none; width: 100%; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .mstats { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .mstats { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  /* Product CTA buttons — Platform Infrastructure orange, Application Delivery green */
  .btn-green  { background: #1E8A4C; color: #fff; }
  .btn-green:hover  { background: #166B3A; }
  .btn-orange { background: #B5551E; color: #fff; }
  .btn-orange:hover { background: #99461A; }
  /* keep both product CTAs on the same baseline regardless of copy length */
  .product-card { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .product-card .btn { margin-top: auto; align-self: flex-start; }
  .sr-only { position:absolute; width:1px; height:1px; padding:0; margin:-1px; overflow:hidden; clip:rect(0,0,0,0); white-space:nowrap; border:0; }

  /* animated SDLC verb — cycles building → testing → securing, resting on shipping.
     The hero script creates each .verb span at runtime, so those nodes never carry
     Astro's scope attribute; match them with :global() inside the scoped slot. */
  .verb-cycle { display:inline-flex; }
  .verb-slot { position:relative; display:inline-block; text-align:left; }
  .verb-sizer { visibility:hidden; }
  .verb-slot :global(.verb) { color:var(--purple); position:absolute; left:0; top:0; opacity:0; transform:translateY(7px); transition:opacity .5s cubic-bezier(.22,.61,.36,1), transform .5s cubic-bezier(.22,.61,.36,1); }
  .verb-slot :global(.verb.is-on) { opacity:1; transform:translateY(0); }
  .verb-slot :global(.verb.is-out) { opacity:0; transform:translateY(-7px); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .verb-slot :global(.verb) { transition:none; } }
  .verb-replay { display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; margin-top:22px; padding:8px 14px; background:transparent; border:1px solid var(--stroke-dark,#38373E); border-radius:var(--r-md,6px); color:var(--neutral-300,#A1A1AA); font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:12px; letter-spacing:0.01em; cursor:pointer; transition:border-color .15s ease, color .15s ease, background-color .15s ease; }
  .verb-replay:hover { border-color:var(--purple); color:#fff; background:rgba(140,100,218,0.08); }
  .verb-replay:disabled { opacity:0.45; cursor:default; }
  .verb-replay .vr-ic { width:14px; height:14px; transition:transform .5s cubic-bezier(.22,.61,.36,1); }
  .verb-replay:not(:disabled):hover .vr-ic { transform:rotate(90deg); }
  .verb-replay:disabled .vr-ic { animation:vr-spin 1.6s linear infinite; }
  @keyframes vr-spin { to { transform:rotate(360deg); } }

  /* Platform section — stacked layers (delivery on foundation) + capability row */
  .platform-stack { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .layer { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr; gap: 32px 40px; align-items: start; border-color: var(--stroke-dark); }
  .layer-main { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .layer-list { align-self: center; }
  .layer-tag { font-size: 12px; color: var(--neutral-500); letter-spacing: .06em; margin-bottom: 6px; }
  /* the foundation reads as a base slab, the delivery layer as the slab resting on it */
  .layer-delivery { border-top: 2px solid var(--green); background: rgba(124,228,131,.035); }
  .layer-foundation { border-top: 2px solid var(--orange); background: rgba(255,131,69,.035); }
  .layer-joint { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 16px; padding: 14px 0; }
  .layer-joint-line { flex: 1; height: 1px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--stroke-dark), transparent); }
  .layer-joint-pill { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--neutral-300); border: 1px solid var(--stroke-dark); border-radius: 999px; padding: 7px 16px; background: var(--ink); white-space: nowrap; }
  .layer-joint-pill svg { width: 14px; height: 14px; color: var(--green); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .layer { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; } .layer-list { align-self: start; } }
  .platform-caps { margin-top: 26px; padding-top: 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--stroke-dark); }
  .platform-caps-lead { display: block; font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--neutral-500); margin-bottom: 16px; padding-left: 2px; }
  .platform-caps-grid { gap: 14px; }
  .cap-card { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; padding: 16px 18px; border: 1px solid var(--stroke-dark); border-radius: var(--r-lg); background: rgba(255,255,255,.02); text-decoration: none; transition: border-color 160ms ease, background 160ms ease, transform 160ms ease; }
  .cap-card:hover { border-color: var(--purple); background: rgba(140,100,218,.08); transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .cap-ic { flex: none; width: 38px; height: 38px; border-radius: var(--r-md); display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; background: rgba(140,100,218,.16); color: #C0A8EF; }
  .cap-ic svg { width: 18px; height: 18px; }
  .cap-body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; min-width: 0; flex: 1; }
  .cap-title { font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; color: #fff; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .cap-desc { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--neutral-400,#9aa0ab); line-height: 1.4; }
  .cap-arrow { flex: none; width: 16px; height: 16px; color: var(--neutral-500); transition: transform 160ms ease, color 160ms ease; }
  .cap-card:hover .cap-arrow { color: #C0A8EF; transform: translateX(3px); }
</style>

<!-- ===================== 1 · HERO ===================== -->
<section class="hero bg-tint-soft">
  <div class="container" style="position:relative;z-index:1">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="slash">//</span> enterprise software delivery</span>
        <h1 class="display-lg" style="white-space:nowrap">The delivery system<br>for teams <span class="verb-cycle" aria-hidden="true"><span class="verb-slot"><span class="verb-sizer" aria-hidden="true">securing</span><span class="verb is-on" data-verb>building</span></span></span><span class="sr-only">shipping</span><br>at AI speed.</h1>
        <p class="body-lg muted pretty" style="max-width:600px">AI writes code faster than most teams can ship it. Ybor closes the gap — production Kubernetes across AWS, Azure, and GCP, from commit to live in minutes, with the audit trail, rollbacks, and SOC 2 controls your security team already requires.</p>
        <div class="hero-ctas">
          <a class="btn btn-primary btn-glow" href="/contact?intent=model">Get started <i data-lucide="arrow-right" class="ic"></i></a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/contact?intent=demo">Book a demo</a>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-note">SOC 2 Type II report <span class="dot">·</span> Multi-cloud <span class="dot">·</span> Built on open source</p>
      </div>

      <!-- product-UI composition -->
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="ui-stack reveal">
          <div style="position:absolute;inset:30px 8px auto 8px;height:180px;border-radius:var(--r-xl);box-shadow:var(--shadow-glow);z-index:0"></div>
          <div class="ui-card" style="position:relative;z-index:1;box-shadow:var(--shadow-lg)">
            <div class="ui-card-head"><i data-lucide="box" style="width:15px;height:15px"></i> platform · <span id="fleetCount">148</span> services</div>
            <div class="ui-card-body">
              {/* 12 identical service cells; the hero script lights them up on scroll-in. */}
              <div class="fleet-grid" id="fleetGrid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,1fr);gap:7px;margin-bottom:14px">
                {Array.from({ length: 12 }).map(() => (
                  <span class="fleet-cell" style="aspect-ratio:1;border-radius:5px;background:rgba(75,171,81,.16);border:1px solid rgba(75,171,81,.55);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center"><span style="width:5px;height:5px;border-radius:999px;background:var(--green-dark);box-shadow:0 0 6px var(--green-dark)"></span></span>
                ))}
              </div>
              <div class="kv"><span class="k">status</span><span class="status-pill status-healthy"><span class="led"></span><span id="fleetHealthy">148 / 148</span> in sync</span></div>
              <div class="kv"><span class="k">clouds</span><span class="v mono" style="font-size:13px">aws · gcp · azure</span></div>
              <div class="kv" style="border-top:1px solid var(--stroke-light);padding-top:12px"><span class="k">platform team</span><span class="v mono" style="font-size:13px;color:var(--green-dark)">unchanged</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ui-card" style="position:relative;z-index:1">
            <div class="ui-card-body" style="padding-top:16px">
              <div class="timeline">
                <div class="tl-item"><span class="tl-mark"><i data-lucide="check"></i></span><span class="tl-line"></span><span class="tl-text">Image scanned — no critical CVEs <span class="when">3m ago</span></span></div>
                <div class="tl-item"><span class="tl-mark"><i data-lucide="check"></i></span><span class="tl-line"></span><span class="tl-text">Kargo gate passed — staging stable 24h <span class="when">2m ago</span></span></div>
                <div class="tl-item"><span class="tl-mark"><i data-lucide="check"></i></span><span class="tl-text"><strong>Deployed to production</strong> · rev a3f9c12 <span class="when">2m ago</span></span></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal" style="position:relative;z-index:1">
            <div class="ui-card-head"><span class="dot-row"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span><span style="margin-left:6px">ybor · cli</span></div>
            <div class="terminal-body"><span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">ybor deploy y-app --env prod</span><br><span class="t-ok">✓ Reconciled</span> <span class="t-dim">· 47s</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== 2 · LOGO BAR ===================== -->
<!-- HIDDEN until we have more customers — restore by removing style="display:none" -->
<section class="section-tight bg-white" style="display:none">
  <div class="container center">
    <p class="label" style="color:var(--neutral-500);margin-bottom:36px">Trusted by enterprise teams</p>
    <div class="logobar-marquee">
      <div class="logobar-track">
        <div class="logobar-group">
          <img class="logo-img tall" src="/assets/logos/ashley.png" alt="Ashley Furniture"><img class="logo-img" src="/assets/logos/linux-foundation.png" alt="Linux Foundation"><img class="logo-img" src="/assets/logos/cncf.svg" alt="CNCF">
        </div>
        <div class="logobar-group" aria-hidden="true">
          <img class="logo-img tall" src="/assets/logos/ashley.png" alt=""><img class="logo-img" src="/assets/logos/linux-foundation.png" alt=""><img class="logo-img" src="/assets/logos/cncf.svg" alt="">
        </div>
        <div class="logobar-group" aria-hidden="true">
          <img class="logo-img tall" src="/assets/logos/ashley.png" alt=""><img class="logo-img" src="/assets/logos/linux-foundation.png" alt=""><img class="logo-img" src="/assets/logos/cncf.svg" alt="">
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== 3 · THE PROBLEM ===================== -->
<section class="section bg-white">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head center">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="slash">//</span> the problem</span>
      <h2 class="display-md balance">An urgent AI mandate. A delivery system that can't keep up.</h2>
      <p class="body-lg muted pretty">Code is ready in minutes; release windows are still weekly. Spend climbs faster than shipped capability, and platform teams are holding it together by hand. None of it is an AI problem — it's a delivery-system problem.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-3" style="margin-top:56px">
      <div class="card reveal">
        <span class="icon-chip"><i data-lucide="gauge"></i></span>
        <p class="label" style="color:var(--neutral-500);margin-bottom:10px">// the velocity gap</p>
        <h3 class="heading-sm" style="margin-bottom:10px">Code ships in minutes. Everything after doesn't.</h3>
        <p class="body muted">Developers ship 5–19× more PRs with AI. Review, tests, and security gates were sized for human throughput — so they queue, get rubber-stamped, or get skipped. The gap between "merged" and "live" now dominates the cycle.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card reveal">
        <span class="icon-chip"><i data-lucide="trending-up"></i></span>
        <p class="label" style="color:var(--neutral-500);margin-bottom:10px">// the leverage gap</p>
        <h3 class="heading-sm" style="margin-bottom:10px">Your product outgrows your platform team every quarter.</h3>
        <p class="body muted">Developer orgs grow faster than the platform teams supporting them. Ticket queues, manual reviews, and bespoke infra keep those teams in reactive work that scales linearly with headcount — so the support gap only widens.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card reveal">
        <span class="icon-chip"><i data-lucide="git-branch"></i></span>
        <p class="label" style="color:var(--neutral-500);margin-bottom:10px">// the governance gap</p>
        <h3 class="heading-sm" style="margin-bottom:10px">Speed without a shared playbook becomes sprawl.</h3>
        <p class="body muted">Every team picks its own AI tools, prompts, and guardrails. No one can answer "what's actually in production," institutional knowledge erodes, and the platform team is the last to know.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== 4 · THE SOLUTION ===================== -->
<section class="section bg-ink-grad">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head center">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="slash">//</span> the platform</span>
      <h2 class="display-md balance">One platform, from infrastructure to production. Built on open source.</h2>
      <p class="body-lg muted-d pretty">Ybor is one platform. It runs your infrastructure — the clusters, policies, secrets, and multi-cloud plumbing — and delivers your applications through it: scaffolding, CI/CD, deployments, rollbacks. Your team owns the source code, the clusters, and the data, on open foundations you can walk away with.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="platform-frame" style="margin-top:56px;border:1px solid var(--stroke-dark);border-radius:var(--r-2xl,24px);background:rgba(255,255,255,.025);padding:clamp(14px,2.4vw,26px)">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:4px 6px 18px">
        <span class="mono" style="font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.04em;color:var(--neutral-300)"><span style="color:var(--purple)">//</span> one platform</span>
        <span class="mono" style="font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.03em;color:var(--neutral-500)">open-source foundations · your clusters, your data</span>
      </div>
      <div class="platform-stack">
        <div class="card dark product-card layer layer-delivery">
          <div class="layer-main">
            <p class="mono layer-tag">LAYER 02 · DELIVERY</p>
            <p class="mono" style="font-size:14px;color:var(--green);letter-spacing:.04em;margin-bottom:16px">APPLICATION DELIVERY</p>
            <h3 class="heading-lg" style="color:#fff;margin-bottom:14px">From commit to production in minutes.</h3>
            <p class="body muted-d" style="margin-bottom:22px">Scaffold a service from a vetted archetype, wire it into CI/CD, ship through ArgoCD and Kargo to staging and prod. Secret injection, service mesh, and policy enforcement come along for the ride.</p>
            <a class="btn btn-primary btn-green" href="/platform#delivery">Explore Application Delivery <i data-lucide="arrow-right" class="ic"></i></a>
          </div>
          <ul class="checklist layer-list">
            <li><i data-lucide="check" class="ck"></i><span>7 archetype families: Java, .NET, Python, Rust, TypeScript, Data/AI, Shared</span></li>
            <li><i data-lucide="check" class="ck"></i><span>CI/CD on GitHub Actions, deploy via ArgoCD + Kargo</span></li>
            <li><i data-lucide="check" class="ck"></i><span>Secret injection via Vault (cloud-native)</span></li>
            <li><i data-lucide="check" class="ck"></i><span>Audit trail and rollback built-in</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="layer-joint" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="layer-joint-line"></span>
          <span class="layer-joint-pill"><i data-lucide="arrow-down"></i> delivery runs on the foundation</span>
          <span class="layer-joint-line"></span>
        </div>

        <div class="card dark product-card layer layer-foundation">
          <div class="layer-main">
            <p class="mono layer-tag">LAYER 01 · FOUNDATION</p>
            <p class="mono" style="font-size:14px;color:var(--orange);letter-spacing:.04em;margin-bottom:16px">PLATFORM INFRASTRUCTURE</p>
            <h3 class="heading-lg" style="color:#fff;margin-bottom:14px">Production infrastructure on day one.</h3>
            <p class="body muted-d" style="margin-bottom:22px">Provision EKS, AKS, and GKE clusters from a single API. Crossplane and Cluster API under the hood. Istio, Kyverno, RBAC, mTLS, and observability wired in by default.</p>
            <a class="btn btn-primary btn-orange" href="/platform#infrastructure">Explore Platform Infrastructure <i data-lucide="arrow-right" class="ic"></i></a>
          </div>
          <ul class="checklist layer-list">
            <li><i data-lucide="check" class="ck"></i><span>Multi-cloud: AWS, Azure, GCP</span></li>
            <li><i data-lucide="check" class="ck"></i><span>Built on Crossplane, Cluster API, Istio, Kyverno</span></li>
            <li><i data-lucide="check" class="ck"></i><span>Object model: Enterprise → Organization → Solution → Application → Environment → Cluster</span></li>
            <li><i data-lucide="check" class="ck"></i><span>SOC 2 controls enforced at the platform layer</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="platform-caps">
        <span class="mono platform-caps-lead">// also part of the platform</span>
        <div class="grid grid-3 platform-caps-grid">
          <a class="cap-card" href="/security">
            <span class="cap-ic"><i data-lucide="shield-check"></i></span>
            <span class="cap-body"><span class="cap-title">Security &amp; Compliance</span><span class="cap-desc">SOC 2, policy-as-code, mTLS, audit</span></span>
            <i data-lucide="arrow-right" class="cap-arrow"></i>
          </a>
          <a class="cap-card" href="/trust-center">
            <span class="cap-ic"><i data-lucide="scale"></i></span>
            <span class="cap-body"><span class="cap-title">Governance</span><span class="cap-desc">Guardrails, RBAC, what's-in-production visibility</span></span>
            <i data-lucide="arrow-right" class="cap-arrow"></i>
          </a>
          <a class="cap-card" href="/how-it-works">
            <span class="cap-ic"><i data-lucide="activity"></i></span>
            <span class="cap-body"><span class="cap-title">Operations &amp; Observability</span><span class="cap-desc">Monitoring, incident response, day-2</span></span>
            <i data-lucide="arrow-right" class="cap-arrow"></i>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== 5 · HOW IT WORKS ===================== -->
<section class="section bg-white" style="position:relative;overflow:hidden">
  <div class="container" style="position:relative;z-index:1">
    <div class="sec-head center">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="slash">//</span> how it works</span>
      <h2 class="display-md balance">Empty repo to production, on one governed path.</h2>
      <p class="body muted pretty">Every service your teams ship follows the same backbone — a layered object model, Kubernetes operators that reconcile it, and an addon catalog on every cluster. Your developers ship; Ybor handles the wiring.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steps" style="margin-top:64px">
      <div class="step"><span class="step-line"></span><div class="step-top"><span class="step-ic"><i data-lucide="layout-template"></i></span><span class="step-num">01</span></div><h4>Scaffold</h4><p>Pick a vetted archetype. One CLI command creates the repo, CI workflow, and base manifests.</p><div class="step-cmd"><span class="p">$</span> <span class="c">archetect render</span></div></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="step-line"></span><div class="step-top"><span class="step-ic"><i data-lucide="git-branch"></i></span><span class="step-num">02</span></div><h4>Commit</h4><p>Push to GitHub. CI runs the matching workflow — test, scan, build, sign.</p><div class="step-cmd"><span class="p">$</span> <span class="c">git push origin main</span></div></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="step-line"></span><div class="step-top"><span class="step-ic"><i data-lucide="boxes"></i></span><span class="step-num">03</span></div><h4>Provision</h4><p>Ybor reconciles Crossplane compositions. New environment, cluster, or namespace — operators handle it.</p><div class="step-cmd"><span class="p">$</span> <span class="c">kubectl apply -f env.yaml</span></div></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="step-line"></span><div class="step-top"><span class="step-ic"><i data-lucide="rocket"></i></span><span class="step-num">04</span></div><h4>Deploy</h4><p>ArgoCD promotes the artifact through environments. Kargo gates each hop on policy, tests, approvals.</p><div class="step-cmd"><span class="p">$</span> <span class="c">argocd app sync</span></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-top"><span class="step-ic"><i data-lucide="activity"></i></span><span class="step-num">05</span></div><h4>Observe</h4><p>OpenTelemetry, Grafana, and Datadog come pre-wired. Audit logs ship to your SIEM.</p><div class="step-cmd"><span class="p">✓</span> <span class="c">traces · live</span></div></div>
